@startuml chart-open-and-live-update-sequence
!theme plain
skinparam wrapWidth 220
title Open a Chart and Receive a Live Candle Update (Dynamic View)

actor User
participant "Terminal UI\n(MarketChart.tsx)" as UI
participant "API/WS Client\n(api.ts)" as Client
participant "REST + WS API\n(main.py)" as API
participant "Market Data Service\n(service.py)" as Service
participant "Live Store\n(store.py)" as Store
participant "Candle Aggregator\n(aggregation.py)" as Aggregator
participant "Database Writer\n(database.py)" as DB
database "TimescaleDB" as TSDB
participant "Exchange Collector\n(exchanges/binance.py)" as Collector
participant "Binance" as Binance

== Initial history load ==
User -> UI : selects exchange,\ninstrument, timeframe
UI -> Client : requestCandles(...)
Client -> API : GET /api/v1/candles\n?exchange&instrumentId&timeframe&limit
API -> Service : get_candles(...)
Service -> DB : query historical candles
DB -> TSDB : SELECT time-series rows
TSDB --> DB : candle rows
DB --> Service : candle history
Service --> API : candle history
API --> Client : 200 OK (candle array)
Client --> UI : render historical candles

== Live stream subscription ==
UI -> Client : openCandleStream(stable)
Client -> API : WS /ws/v1/candles/stable\n?exchange&instrumentId&timeframe
API -> Store : subscribe(stream key)
Store --> API : ack subscription

== Live trade arrives and propagates ==
Binance -> Collector : trade event (WS push)
Collector -> Service : normalized Trade
Service -> Aggregator : update_candle(trade)
Aggregator -> Aggregator : apply revision rules,\napply stable-chart delay
Aggregator -> Store : publish revised 1s candle
Aggregator -> DB : persist candle revision
DB -> TSDB : UPSERT candle row
Store -> API : notify subscribers\n(revision changed)
API -> Client : WS push: updated candle
Client -> UI : merge live candle\ninto chart series
UI --> User : chart updates\nnear real time

note over Aggregator, Store
  Only changed revisions are pushed
  (ADR-003); provisional candles are
  flagged separately from stable ones
end note

@enduml
